    <innerclass refid="classClinicControllerBase" prot="public">ClinicControllerBase</innerclass>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Abstract contract for clinic-service entity handlers (patients, visits, reports, prescriptions, ...). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Declares <computeroutput><ref refid="classClinicControllerBase" kindref="compound">ClinicControllerBase</ref></computeroutput>, a pure interface for clinical data. It keeps the subset of CRUDS that makes sense for medical records and adds GetVisits for a patient&apos;s visit history. As with the other bases, every operation is pure virtual (<computeroutput>= 0</computeroutput>) and answers through a CALLBACK_.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: Clinical entities do not all support the same actions: for example, only <ref refid="classPatient" kindref="compound">Patient</ref> and <ref refid="classVisits" kindref="compound">Visits</ref> can be deleted, and only <ref refid="classPatient" kindref="compound">Patient</ref> supports search and visit lookup. This interface defines the common surface the HTTP layer can rely on, while letting the concrete <ref refid="classClinicController" kindref="compound">ClinicController</ref> return a clear &quot;not implemented&quot; for unsupported actions. Without it, clinic endpoints would have no uniform contract.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Virtual functions / abstract classes: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/abstract_class">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/abstract_class</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Callback / std::function: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/functional/function">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/functional/function</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Coroutines (co_await / drogon::Task): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/coroutines">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/coroutines</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::optional (an id that may be missing): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Namespaces and <computeroutput>using namespace</computeroutput>: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/namespace">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/namespace</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
